{"name":"Money Banks","hex":"#aabe49","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"money","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A generally accepted means of exchange.","A currency maintained by a state or other entity which can guarantee its value (such as a monetary union). (Can we clean up this sense?)"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cool; excellent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/money"},{"term":"banks","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of bank"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of bank"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/banks"}],"entries":[{"title":"Money","blocks":[{"text":"Money is any item or verifiable record that is generally accepted as payment for goods and services and repayment of debts, such as taxes, in a particular country or socio-economic context. The primary functions which distinguish money are: medium of exchange, a unit of account, a store of value and sometimes, a standard of deferred payment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Euro_coins_and_banknotes_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Euro_coins_and_banknotes_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Money","wikidata":"Q1368"},{"title":"Bank","blocks":[{"text":"A bank is a financial institution that accepts deposits from the public and creates a demand deposit while making loans. Lending activities can be directly performed by the bank or indirectly through capital markets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/London.bankofengland.arp.jpg/330px-London.bankofengland.arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bank","wikidata":"Q22687"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/BMC_06.jpg/330px-BMC_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikiped